WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
Your heart muscle contracts
with every beat of your life,

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.390
and it does not fatigue.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.520
Now sprint flat out.

4
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:11.400
Within seconds, some of your
leg muscle starts to fatigue.

5
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:16.320
In one set of illustrative data, two
muscles were stimulated again and again for

6
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.870
60 seconds.

7
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.460
One kept 92 per cent
of its starting force.

8
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.410
The other fell to 25 per cent.

9
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.840
Both are muscle.

10
00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.880
So what makes the difference?

11
00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.950
In this mission, you'll compare
different kinds of muscle,

12
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.450
side by side.

13
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.710
Then you'll explain why each kind
of muscle is built the way it is.

14
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:41.760
Your mission: find out what lets some
muscle work all your life without tiring,

15
00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.040
while some gives out in seconds.
